# APPEND-ONLY LEDGERS: union merge.
#
# Measured 2026-07-27 (results/telemetry_ledger_rewrite.md): two sessions that
# each append one row to the same ledger produce a textual conflict at the
# tail, because both add a different line in the same place.  Nothing about
# that is a real disagreement -- the file's whole contract is that rows
# accumulate -- so `union` takes both sides, which is exactly what an
# append-only ledger means.
#
# Every file listed here is written ONLY through a tool that opens it in
# append mode ("a"), never rewritten:
#   tools/cycle_telemetry.py:179   tools/lessons.py:152
#   tools/frontier_refusals.py:480 tools/frontier_parks.py:105
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED: results/formalize_bench_state.jsonl and every
# other results/*.jsonl that regen_downstream REGENERATES.  A regenerated
# artifact under union merge would accumulate both sides' full contents --
# silent duplication, which is worse than the conflict it avoids.  This list
# is per-file rather than a results/*.jsonl glob for exactly that reason: a
# new ledger must be added here deliberately, after checking how it is
# written.
#
# Union can introduce a duplicate row if both sides append an identical one;
# tests/test_cycle_telemetry.py::test_committed_ledger_is_append_shaped is
# the tooth that catches that on the telemetry ledgers.
results/cycle_telemetry_corpus.jsonl     merge=union
results/cycle_telemetry_purchase.jsonl   merge=union
results/cycle_telemetry_watchdog.jsonl   merge=union
results/lessons.jsonl                    merge=union
results/frontier_refusals.jsonl          merge=union
results/frontier_parks.jsonl             merge=union
